From: martino@gomez.Jpl.Nasa.Gov (Martin R. Olah)
Subject: Oceania 

New Countries will not work in the foreseeable future unless they drop the 
New Country spiel.
 
"How To Start Your Own Country" clearly documents the disasterous effects
of claiming independence. Forming a community in a remote area would work a
lot better if people didn't feel the need to trumpet their secession.
  As I mentioned before, The Atlantis Project should have tried to acquire
the Saigon Floating Hotel or raised real money from real investors in order
to build another. I believe having a serious resort, fish-farm, whatever, is a 
prerequisite. You can always hire libertarians, rent/sell accomodations,
and otherwise slowly build up a free community.

An in-your-face secession will assuredly sink the whole project, regardless
of money raised. As such is the case, I would recommend building within or
over a coral atoll. This would provide some measure of protection physically,
and legally as well, if the location is far enough away from any other claims.
Of course this would have a negative effect on mobility.

Despite my doubts I respect all attempts at freedom, and monitor their results
with interest.

                            O Martin

